    </namestyle>
    <!-- Qud's name generation is very nearly gender-blind: exactly one namestyle in the whole
         vanilla file uses a Gender attribute. What reads as male-coded is a phonetic property of
         the postfix pool - 23 of vanilla's 24 endings are hard stops, `la` being the only open
         one. The ending carries almost all of the gendered read, so it is the lever.

         117 of the 126 blueprints that resolve to Qudish inherit RandomGender="male,female"
         from BaseHuman - a coin flip rolled before the name is generated. So half of every
         generated human already IS female, and was drawing from the hard-stop pool.

         Species="human" is load-bearing. A scope carrying only Gender matches every female
         creature in the game, and female bears would draw Qudish names.

         Priority 50 is load-bearing too. Exclusion is `other.priority > scope.priority`, and the
         faction namestyles that must keep winning - Templar, Barathrumite, Mechanimist, Snapjaw -
         sit at exactly 100 with Combine="false". At 100 this would displace them instead of
         losing to them. naming-priority holds the ceiling. -->
    <namestyle Name="Vixy_Qudish Feminine" Format="TitleCase">
      <scopes>
        <!-- The player-facing half. mod/Scripting/Vixy_NameFlavourModule.cs replaces the
           random player name at BOOTEVENT_GENERATERANDOMPLAYERNAME, passing the Tag the player
           asked for - which is the only way to reach a character whose name is generated before
           the character exists.

           Priority 200 with Combine="false" because an explicit choice should win outright.
           Vixy_Random is Priority 50 and combines instead: all three namestyles carry it at the
           same priority, so the weighted draw splits evenly between them, which is what "random"
           means here rather than a fourth pool. -->
        <scope Name="Vixy_Femme" Tag="Vixy_Femme" Priority="200" Combine="false" />
        <scope Name="Vixy_Random" Tag="Vixy_Random" Priority="50" Combine="true" />
        <scope Name="Vixy_Gender" Species="human" Gender="female" Priority="50" Combine="true" />
      </scopes>
      <prefixes Amount="1">
        <prefix Name="ae" />
        <prefix Name="be" />
        <prefix Name="ce" />
        <prefix Name="dho" />
        <prefix Name="el" />
        <prefix Name="en" />
